---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalHero from '../../components/LegalHero.astro';
import { COMPANY, path } from '../../i18n/config';

const locale = 'en' as const;
---

<Base
  locale={locale}
  page="terms"
  title="Terms and conditions — Belgium Cleaning Facilities"
  description="General terms of service of Belgium Cleaning Facilities (BCF) for its business clients."
>
  <LegalHero eyebrow="Terms and conditions" title="General terms of service" updated="Last updated: 1 September 2026" />

  <article class="prose-legal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2>1. Purpose and scope</h2>
    <p>
      These general terms govern the business relationship between <strong>{COMPANY.legalName}</strong> ("BCF"),
      {COMPANY.address}, and its business clients, for any cleaning service ordered on the basis of an accepted
      quote. BCF does not work with private individuals.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Quotes and orders</h2>
    <p>
      Any quote issued by BCF is free of charge and valid for 30 days from its issue date, unless stated otherwise.
      An order is considered firm once the client accepts the quote in writing (signature, confirmation email, or
      purchase order).
    </p>

    <h2>3. Performance of services</h2>
    <p>
      BCF undertakes to perform the services with the care and diligence of a professional in the sector, in
      compliance with applicable safety standards, in particular VCA certification. Stated intervention timelines
      are indicative and may be adjusted depending on site access conditions, weather conditions (for outdoor or
      high-level work) or force majeure.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Client obligations</h2>
    <p>
      The client undertakes to provide safe and compliant access to the intervention site, to notify BCF in advance
      of any specific constraints (sensitive areas, specific hours, required permits or clearances), and, where
      applicable, to provide the water and electricity points needed to carry out the service.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Pricing and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are stated in euros, excluding VAT unless stated otherwise. Unless otherwise agreed in the quote,
      invoices are payable within 30 calendar days of the invoice date. Late payment may give rise to late-payment
      interest and a fixed compensation fee, in accordance with Belgian legislation on combating late payment in
      commercial transactions.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Insurance and liability</h2>
    <p>
      BCF holds professional civil liability insurance covering its cleaning activities. BCF's liability may only be
      engaged in the event of proven fault in the performance of the services, and is limited to direct damages,
      excluding any indirect or immaterial damage.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Recurring maintenance contracts</h2>
    <p>
      For recurring maintenance services covered by a contract, either party may terminate it subject to the
      written notice period agreed in the contract or, failing that, a reasonable notice period of at least 30
      days.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      Any complaint relating to a service must be sent to BCF in writing, within a reasonable time following
      performance of the relevant service, to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Applicable law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      These general terms are governed by Belgian law. Any dispute relating to their interpretation or performance
      falls under the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of the judicial district of BCF's registered office,
      subject to any mandatory legal provisions to the contrary.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also our <a href={path('legal', locale)}>legal notice</a> and our
      <a href={path('privacy', locale)}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
